map-web/2","section":3,"section_title":"Dyadic localization and its information cost","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:def400376273986bd0473af50771493b9ab2a4277a53c467dd6ab052b2325bde","file":"preprints/Localization-costs-and-information-growth-for-exact-Gaussian-observations-September-27-2026/build/sections/02-dyadic.tex","line":54,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"6a0a361b5ab5ded0626bd7dc4895b2463c9ed89143fcf9767255f793039aecf7","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Localization-costs-and-information-growth-for-exact-Gaussian-observations-September-27-2026/build/sections/02-dyadic.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:def400376273986bd0473af50771493b9ab2a4277a53c467dd6ab052b2325bde","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Localization-costs-and-information-growth-for-exact-Gaussian-observations-September-27-2026/build/sections/02-dyadic.tex#L54"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{ld:thm:main}\nThere is an absolute constant $c>0$ with the following property.\nFor any fixed $C_0>0$, consider the experiment above with $t\\ge0$\nblocks and $N\\ge1$ possible message values, and suppose\n\\begin{equation}\\label{ld:eq:alphabet}\n \\bigl(2/m+e^{-ck}\\bigr)\\log N\\le C_0d.\n\\end{equation}\nOne can reveal nested dyadic cells\n$Q_0\\supset Q_1\\supset\\cdots\\supset Q_t$ containing $Z$, where $Q_i$\nis a finite-valued measurable function of $Z$, the preceding revelations,\nand $W_1,\\ldots,W_i$, so that the augmented transcript\n\\[\n \\Pi_t=(W_1,Q_1,\\ldots,W_t,Q_t)\n\\]\nsatisfies\n\\begin{equation}\\label{ld:eq:main}\n I(Z;\\Pi_t)\\le Cdt.\n\\end{equation}\nHere $C$ is a constant depending only on $C_0$. If $J_t$ is the level of $Q_t$, the\nconstruction also gives $\\E J_t\\le Ct$."}
